sues/118908","id":4320673370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYg-Wg","user":{"login":"Kry0000","id":119920576,"node_id":"U_kgDOByXXwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119920576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000","html_url":"https://github.com/Kry0000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T22:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T22:01:55Z","body":"I'm new Bisecting but I'm pretty sure I did it correctly, following Godot's Contributor Docs on the matter and here's my result:\n```\n5f8f0ac3053e5e7eee6dbfc40b336c4d4e52f147 is the first bad commit\ncommit 5f8f0ac3053e5e7eee6dbfc40b336c4d4e52f147 (HEAD)\nAuthor: Airyzz <36567925+Airyzz@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Jun 5 18:03:43 2025 +0930\n\n    [web] add support for pen pressure\n\n platform/web/display_server_web.cpp         | 9 +++++----\n platform/web/display_server_web.h           | 4 ++--\n platform/web/godot_js.h                     | 2 +-\n platform/web/js/libs/library_godot_input.js | 4 ++--\n 4 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320673370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320755287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118908#issuecomment-4320755287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118908","id":4320755287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYl-Vw","user":{"login":"Kry0000","id":119920576,"node_id":"U_kgDOByXXwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119920576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000","html_url":"https://github.com/Kry0000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T22:56:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T22:56:50Z","body":"I changed to the commit ```5f8f0ac3053e5e7eee6dbfc40b336c4d4e52f147```\nFigured out that the change that they did, changing the file at this path ```platform/web/js/libs/library_godot_input.js``` at line ```520```, and the code:\n```\nGodotEventListeners.add(window, 'mousemove', move_cb, false);\n```\nto\n```\nGodotEventListeners.add(window, 'pointermove', move_cb, false);\n```\ncauses the bug.\n\nAfter changing back the string ```'pointermove'``` to ```'mousemove'``` the bug is fixed.\n\nThough I'm pretty sure this breaks what the commit was trying to add, as the Output now states that ```pressure=NaN``` or ```pressure=nan``` I don't remember if it was upper-cased or not.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320755287/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320951391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118908#issuecomment-4320951391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118908","id":4320951391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYx8Xw","user":{"login":"Kry0000","id":119920576,"node_id":"U_kgDOByXXwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119920576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000","html_url":"https://github.com/Kry0000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T01:01:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T01:01:30Z","body":"Testing on a basic local HTML file with some inline javascript, the event ```pointermove``` seems to fire even when the mouse is not moving. It has the same \"issue\" as the bug stated.\n\nReading up on the event, here are 2 sources I've read:\n\n1. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/pointermove_event\n2. https://w3c.github.io/pointerevents/#the-pointermove-event\n\nThe the link for W3C states this for ```pointermove```:\n\nThe ```user agent``` MUST ```fire a pointer event``` named ```pointermove``` when a pointer changes any properties that don't fire ```pointerdown``` or ```pointerup``` events. This includes any changes to coordinates, pressure, tangential pressure, tilt, twist, contact geometry (width and height) or ```chorded buttons```.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320951391/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320976912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118908#issuecomment-4320976912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118908","id":4320976912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYzgEA","user":{"login":"Kry0000","id":119920576,"node_id":"U_kgDOByXXwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119920576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000","html_url":"https://github.com/Kry0000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T01:17:25Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T01:17:25Z","body":"My consensus is that Godot is not to blame for this behavior, rather it's the browser's implementation of the ```pointermove``` event and how it decides to fire.\n\nMy suggestion would be to put back ```mousemove``` and put ```pointermove``` as it's own ```InputEvent``` instead of tying it to ```InputEventMouseMotion```, maybe something like ```InputEventPointerMotion```, but that sounds confusing and too similar to ```InputEventMouseMotion```.\n\nI don't know, I'll leave it to the more seasoned developers to figure out a solution.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320976912/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4321121154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118908#issuecomment-4321121154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118908","id":4321121154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAY8Tgg","user":{"login":"Kry0000","id":119920576,"node_id":"U_kgDOByXXwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119920576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000","html_url":"https://github.com/Kry0000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kry0000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T02:52:58Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T02:52:58Z","body":"> Related (specifically for Windows):\n> \n>     * [InputEventMouseMotion is generated after each mouse button release #20357](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/20357)\n\nFrom my research, it does not seem related, my fault for not getting more information and digging deeper before posting. Sorry.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4321121154/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]